<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Fog on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/fog/</link><description>Recent content in Fog on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:45:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/fog/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Morning Mist at the Pool</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/morning-mist-at-the-pool/</link><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:45:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/morning-mist-at-the-pool/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Took this walking to the swimming pool this morning. The fog was sitting low over the field, backlit by the rising sun and cutting the trees off at the knees. Found it very atmospheric, almost other worldly.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="wp-caption alignnone"&gt;&#10; &lt;a data-flickr-embed="true" data-header="true" data-footer="false"&#10; data-context="false"&#10; href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/55520347637"&#10; title="Morning Mist"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/55520347637_d3d372b593_z.jpg" width="800" alt="Morning Mist" /&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;script async src="//embedr.flickr.com/assets/client-code.js" charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="wp-caption-text"&gt;Fog sitting low over the field on the way to the pool, backlit by the rising sun.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;</description></item><item><title>Day 299 freezing frog</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-299-freezing-frog/</link><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jan 2014 06:55:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-299-freezing-frog/</guid><description>&lt;div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'&gt;&lt;img style='max-width:586px;' src='http://farm6.staticflickr.com/5473/12064729263_9af9a922df_b.jpg'/&gt;&